---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Why reform is needed" description="Why UnPoison advocates for stronger pesticide safeguards, transparent evidence and practical alternatives in South Africa.">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-current="page">Why reform is needed</span></nav>
    <p class="eyebrow">The case for change</p>
    <h1>Why reform is needed</h1>
    <p class="lede">How pesticides are registered and used affects farmworkers, nearby communities, water, soil and wildlife. UnPoison is calling for stronger safeguards and safer ways to manage pests.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule">
    <div class="shell work-grid">
      <div class="work-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">The framework</p>
        <h2>The law and its limits.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="article-body">
        <p><a href="https://www.gov.za/documents/fertilizers-farm-feeds-seeds-and-remedies-act-28-may-2015-1101">Act 36 of 1947</a> still governs pesticide registration in South Africa. It has been amended, but UnPoison argues that registration, monitoring and restrictions need to better protect people and ecosystems.</p>
        <p>We are calling for tighter controls on highly hazardous pesticides, public access to registration information and a practical route to safer alternatives.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="video-feature-band section-rule" aria-labelledby="reform-video-title">
    <div class="shell video-feature">
      <a class="video-feature-media" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yxWBprX6KmM" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch UnPoison Our Air on YouTube (opens in a new tab)">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yxWBprX6KmM/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
        <span class="video-play-mark" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
      </a>
      <div class="video-feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Watch: spray drift</p>
        <h2 id="reform-video-title">Exposure does not stop at the field boundary.</h2>
        <p>UnPoison Our Air examines how pesticide spray can drift beyond treated fields and affect nearby communities.</p>
        <a class="line-link line-link-light" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yxWBprX6KmM" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch on YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Where we focus</p><h2>Three priorities for reform.</h2></div>
        <p class="lede">Our work spans national pesticide rules and local spraying practices.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="action-routes">
        <a class="action-route" href="/resources/hhp-database-2025/"><span class="number">01</span><span><h3>Identify highly hazardous pesticides</h3><p>Explore UnPoison's 2025 list of highly hazardous pesticides legally in use.</p></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-route" href="/resources/biopesticide-regulatory-gaps-2026/"><span class="number">02</span><span><h3>Make room for safer alternatives</h3><p>We propose a separate registration process for biopesticides.</p></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-route" href="/campaigns/pesticide-free-cape-town/"><span class="number">03</span><span><h3>Stop routine roadside spraying</h3><p>The Cape Town campaign helps communities replace herbicide spraying with non-chemical weed control.</p></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
